// Control and base rate for onprem_password_events.kql: every account that reset
// or unlocked someone else's password on this domain in 30 days. An admin who
// does this routinely is the helpdesk; a reset by an account that never does it is
// the finding. A zero here means the DC Security log is not collected, so the
// subject's zero is a gap, not a negative.
WindowsAudit
| where timestamp > ago(30d)
| where toint(EventID) in (4724, 4767)
| summarize actions = count(), targets = dcount(tostring(TargetUserName)),
    firstSeen = min(timestamp), lastSeen = max(timestamp)
    by Admin = tostring(SubjectUserName), EventID = toint(EventID)
| order by actions desc
| take 1000
